„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections™…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ0The word of the LORD came unto me again, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›What mean ye, that ye use this proverb concerning the land of Israel, saying, The fathers have eaten sour grapes, and the children's teeth are set on edge?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaAs I live, saith the Lord GOD, ye shall not have occasion any more to use this proverb in Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€Behold, all souls are mine; as the soul of the father, so also the soul of the son is mine: the soul that sinneth, it shall die.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse	¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ<But if a man be just, and do that which is lawful and right,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÄand hath not eaten upon the mountains, neither hath lifted up his eyes to the idols of the house of Israel, neither hath defiled his neighbour's wife, neither hath come near to a menstruous woman,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙµand hath not oppressed any, but hath restored to the debtor his pledge, hath spoiled none by violence, hath given his bread to the hungry, and hath covered the naked with a garment;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¦he that hath not given forth upon usury, neither hath taken any increase, that hath withdrawn his hand from iniquity, hath executed true judgment between man and man,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|hath walked in my statutes, and hath kept my judgments, to deal truly; he is just, he shall surely live, saith the Lord GOD.¦layout ªlast_verse	…¤book§chapter«first_verse
