¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkIf he beget a son that is a robber, a shedder of blood, and that doeth the like to any one of these things,¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqand that doeth not any of those duties, but even hath eaten upon the mountains, and defiled his neighbour's wife,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ hath oppressed the poor and needy, hath spoiled by violence, hath not restored the pledge, and hath lifted up his eyes to the idols, hath committed abomination,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ³hath given forth upon usury, and hath taken increase: shall he then live? he shall not live: he hath done all these abominations; he shall surely die; his blood shall be upon him.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzNow, lo, if he beget a son, that seeth all his father's sins which he hath done, and considereth, and doeth not such like,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“that hath not eaten upon the mountains, neither hath lifted up his eyes to the idols of the house of Israel, hath not defiled his neighbour's wife,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ°neither hath oppressed any, hath not withholden the pledge, neither hath spoiled by violence, but hath given his bread to the hungry, and hath covered the naked with a garment,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÕthat hath taken off his hand from the poor, that hath not received usury nor increase, hath executed my judgments, hath walked in my statutes; he shall not die for the iniquity of his father, he shall surely live.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ©As for his father, because he cruelly oppressed, spoiled his brother by violence, and did that which is not good among his people, lo, even he shall die in his iniquity.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÂYet say ye, Why? doth not the son bear the iniquity of the father? When the son hath done that which is lawful and right, and hath kept all my statutes, and hath done them, he shall surely live.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙøThe soul that sinneth, it shall die. The son shall not bear the iniquity of the father, neither shall the father bear the iniquity of the son: the righteousness of the righteous shall be upon him, and the wickedness of the wicked shall be upon him.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ®But if the wicked will turn from all his sins that he hath committed, and keep all my statutes, and do that which is lawful and right, he shall surely live, he shall not die.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠAll his transgressions that he hath committed, they shall not be mentioned unto him: in his righteousness that he hath done he shall live.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHave I any pleasure at all that the wicked should die? saith the Lord GOD: and not that he should return from his ways, and live?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚMBut when the righteous turneth away from his righteousness, and committeth iniquity, and doeth according to all the abominations that the wicked man doeth, shall he live? All his righteousness that he hath done shall not be mentioned: in his trespass that he hath trespassed, and in his sin that he hath sinned, in them shall he die.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzYet ye say, The way of the Lord is not equal. Hear now, O house of Israel; Is not my way equal? are not your ways unequal?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–When a righteous man turneth away from his righteousness, and committeth iniquity, and dieth in them; for his iniquity that he hath done shall he die.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›Again, when the wicked man turneth away from his wickedness that he hath committed, and doeth that which is lawful and right, he shall save his soul alive.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„Because he considereth, and turneth away from all his transgressions that he hath committed, he shall surely live, he shall not die.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…Yet saith the house of Israel, The way of the Lord is not equal. O house of Israel, are not my ways equal? are not your ways unequal?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÁTherefore I will judge you, O house of Israel, every one according to his ways, saith the Lord GOD. Repent, and turn yourselves from all your transgressions; so iniquity shall not be your ruin.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙœCast away from you all your transgressions, whereby ye have transgressed; and make you a new heart and a new spirit: for why will ye die, O house of Israel?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrFor I have no pleasure in the death of him that dieth, saith the Lord GOD: wherefore turn yourselves, and live ye.¦layout ªlast_verse 